     "body": "<p>Hi Joseph, Andrew,</p>\n\n<p>That translation of the ontology is a pretty nice representation of the ontology (thanks for the link!) in JSON-LD, but the context part is just the namespaces at the top.  The rest of the document (@graph and below) would be ignored by a context processor.  A full context would also likely map the predicates into more JSONic (is that a word?) keys.</p>\n\n<p>I'll build a full context for PCDM and make a PR to the git repo with it <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/>  Then we can re-discuss what names are appropriate for different classes and predicates <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/wink.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/></p>",
     "created": "08/Jul/15 11:51 AM",
